<h2 id="integration-heading">Pallet Conveyor Integration</h2>
<h3>Palletizer Integration</h3>
<p>Pallet conveyors transport empty pallets to <a href="/industries/packaging-line-conveyors/pallet/">palletizers</a> and loaded pallets away. <a href="/industries/packaging-line-conveyors/pallet/pallet-dispenser/">Pallet dispensers</a> feed empty pallets onto the infeed conveyor. Outfeed conveyors transport loaded pallets to stretch wrap and shipping. Conveyor height must match the palletizer infeed and discharge height. Pallet conveyors are usually built low so forklifts and pallet jacks can load them. Arrow Conveyor, for example, lists a standard top-of-chain height of 12" to 24" for its CDLR pallet conveyor (<a href="https://www.arrowconveyor.com/product/chain-driven-live-roller-pallet-conveyor/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Arrow Conveyor</a>).</p>
<h3>Stretch Wrapper Integration</h3>
<p>Pallet conveyors feed stretch wrappers and remove wrapped pallets. Turntable wrappers require a powered turntable or transfer to position the pallet. Chain transfers such as Alba's use a pneumatic four-point lift and are rated up to 4,000 lb (<a href="https://www.albamfg.com/products/chain-transfers/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Alba chain transfers</a>). Rotary arm and ring wrappers allow in-line pallet flow without transfer. Conveyor speed must match wrapper cycle time.</p>
<h3>AS/RS Integration</h3>
<p>Automated storage and retrieval systems (AS/RS) interface with pallet conveyors at pick/deposit stations. Conveyors queue pallets for crane pickup and receive pallets from crane deposits. Zone accumulation controls pallet flow to match crane cycle. Pallet verification (dimensions, weight, label) often occurs on the conveyor before AS/RS entry.</p>
<h3>Dock Operations</h3>
<p>Pallet conveyors transport pallets between production/storage and shipping docks. Gravity pallet flow lanes stage pallets in order. Powered conveyors extend into truck trailers for automated trailer loading systems (ATLS). Dock levelers and vehicle restraints integrate with <a href="/industries/mining-conveyors/">conveyor safety systems</a>.</p>
