<h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="usa-accordion usa-accordion--bordered usa-accordion--multiselectable" data-allow-multiple="">
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-1">What is a pallet conveyor?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-1" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>A pallet conveyor is a heavy-duty conveyor designed to transport loaded pallets. Pallet conveyors use <a href="/conveyor-types/cdlr-conveyors/">CDLR</a>, <a href="/conveyor-types/chain-conveyors/">drag chain</a>, or heavy-duty roller systems. They integrate with <a href="/industries/packaging-line-conveyors/pallet/">palletizers</a>, stretch wrappers, and AS/RS systems.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-2">What type of conveyor is used for pallets?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-2" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>The most common types are <a href="/conveyor-types/cdlr-conveyors/">CDLR</a> for standard pallets, <a href="/conveyor-types/chain-conveyors/">drag chain</a> for heavy or non-standard pallets, <a href="/conveyor-types/roller-conveyors/gravity/">heavy-duty gravity roller</a> for pallet flow, and <a href="/conveyor-types/transfer-conveyors/">turntables or chain transfers</a> for direction changes. CDLR is the standard for most applications.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-3">How much weight can a pallet conveyor handle?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-3" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>It depends on the model. Alba rates some <a href="/conveyor-types/cdlr-conveyors/">CDLR</a> models up to 15,000 lb and its standard <a href="/conveyor-types/chain-conveyors/">drag chain</a> conveyor up to 6,000 lb. Titan rates CDLR rollers from 250 lb to 2,500 lb per roller. Capacity depends on roller diameter, spacing, bearing rating, chain size, and frame construction. Always specify maximum expected load plus safety factor.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-4">What is the difference between CDLR and drag chain?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-4" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p><a href="/conveyor-types/cdlr-conveyors/">CDLR</a> uses chain-driven rollers that contact pallet bottom boards. Works best with standard pallets. <a href="/conveyor-types/chain-conveyors/">Drag chain</a> uses chain strands that directly contact pallet stringers. Handles skids, non-standard sizes, and bottoms that do not convey well on rollers.</p>

</div>
</div>
